1. Free to use, fork, and modify. Even competing products built with this code are free up to $1 million in revenue a year, with only a small 3% fee beyond that $1 million.

Use it freely

Use this software for personal projects or inside your business,
regardless of your company's size or revenue. Copy it, modify it,
and keep your modifications private. None of that requires payment,
registration, or reporting.

You can also sell work you create using this software. Using it as
a tool does not, by itself, make that work subject to this license
or require you to share its revenue. Selling noncompeting products
and services is also free of the payment condition below. Section
2 defines what counts as competing.

Compete with us, too

You may sell this software, build products from it, or offer its
functionality as a hosted service. You may compete directly with us.
You do not need separate permission, and you do not have to publish
your source code.

We welcome competition. We also want to keep working on this
software without being driven out of business by someone selling
it against us. So there is one additional condition: the first
US $1,000,000 in annual Covered Revenue from competing products and
services is yours. Above that, you pay us 3% of the excess.

Keep the notices

Keep the copyright and license notices with copies of this
software, including substantial portions incorporated into other
software. This does not apply to work merely created using it.

The details

Under that line You owe nothing and condition (b) of Section 2 is
satisfied for the year with no act on Your part: nothing to pay,
report, register, or notify. Keep the copyright notice in copies,
as condition (a) requires, and You are finished with this license.
The line is tested year by year, so look again once a year. If You
are not sure whether something You sell is covered, Section 5
makes the answer free and binding within 30 days.

Crossing the line never makes the first US $1,000,000 payable,
never reaches back into an earlier year, and never ends this
license. Sections 4 through 6 say how Covered Revenue is counted
and the fee is paid. This section describes the condition; Section
2 states it and Sections 4 through 6 measure it. Where this
section and those differ, those govern, and nothing in this
section creates an obligation they do not.


